Date: Tue, 15 Feb 1994 19:31:34 GMT

  I have tried to get information about games playing from the EFF archives.
  The archive-manager has told me that at this time a problem with the
  archive-server prevents this.  At Indiana State University, we are
  looking afresh at the problem of game playing -- especially interactive
  game playing over the Internet -- at University microcomputer lab work-
  stations.

  The following is a first draft of A STATEMENT OF PRINCIPLES on
  APPROPRIATE USE OF COMPUTER FACILITIES to guide our consideration of
  this situation.  Comments?

DRAFT      DRAFT     DRAFT     DRAFT     DRAFT     DRAFT     DRAFT     DRAFT

1.   The computer and telecommunications facilities of the Indiana
     State University are resources supported by public funds and
     by student tuition and fees and are intended to support the
     scholarly mission of the University.

2.   The President, Vice-Presidents, and other Administrators are
     stewards of the resources of the University and are responsible
     for their appropriate use.  This responsibility extends to the
     establishment of appropriate use policies and procedures, and
     for the enforcement of these policies and procedures within the
     University community.

3.   The University is a community of scholars -- faculty, students,
     and administrators -- all of whom have an interest in the
     appropriate use of computer and telecommunications facilities,
     and whose concerns must be considered in the development
     of policies and procedures for appropriate use.

DRAFT      DRAFT     DRAFT     DRAFT     DRAFT     DRAFT     DRAFT     DRAFT
-------------------------------------------------
HAL CHENEY -- Indiana State University Libraries
